<div class="c"><h1 class="redstar">Poetry By:Amanda-Gwen</h1></div><h2 class="c">Miserable Life</h2><p>candlelight flickers against the walls<br>releasing my demons<br>they play and entertain me<br>while sleep crawls across my eyes<br>dreams want to seep into my mind<br>music drifts out to me<br>singing sad melodies<br><br>as the bottle of pills fall from my hand<br>the bottle of pills fall from my hand<br><br><br> a lifetime of memories<br>now a fuel for my agony<br>too many mistakes have been made<br>no use I cry out against the pain<br>andthe injustices that life had relayed<br>and yet I've wallowed in the pain<br>thinking there's something to be gained<br><br><br>but now that bottle of pills fall from my hand<br>the bottle of pills fall from my hand<br><br><br> I whisper my good-bye<br>for very soon I will die<br>I think of all the loves gone bye<br>how they rejected me<br>Oh, now I will know my pain<br>in the journal before me I bared my shame<br><br><br>before the bottle of pills fell from my hands<br>the bottle of pills fell from my hand<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Lies</h2><p>I thought you were an angel<br>    come to rescue me<br>    When you came into my life<br>    I was tired of the lonely nights<br>    alone, under moonlit skies<br>    just never thinking I'd fall in love<br>  </p>  but now the winds blow cold tonight<br>  the blue in the sky falls onto my head<br>  I'd rather risk never holding love again<br>  than to give in to you<br>  but, oh<br>  <p> the lies<br>    the sweet little lies<br>    made our love a paradise<br>    yet like Adam and Eve<br>    I was deceived<br>    by your lies<br>    your sweet little lies<br>    I took a chance thought I was blind<br>    and held on to your every line<br>    I just couldn't help but fall<br>    and throw away my chances to be free<br>    from your lies<br>  </p>  the days they've gotten long<br>  I wish you had never left me<br>  or met me<br>  for I can never shake the memories<br>  of all those sinful things you did with me<br>  but, oh<br>  <p> all those lies<br>    those sick twisted lies<br>    that took my soul<br>    before you said good-bye<br>    it hurt so bad yet felt so nice<br>    making me desire<br>    more of your sweet-lipped lies<br>    oh, no<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"></body>
